module

public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Adjunction.ReflectiveRestriction
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.Pushforward
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FormalGeometry.DerivedCompletionRinged.ReflectorCompletion
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# Derived direct image on the derived-complete objects

Let `f : (Sh(𝒟), 𝒪') ⟶ (Sh(𝒞), 𝒪)` be a morphism of ringed sites and let `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪`, `ℐ' ⊂ 𝒪'` be
sheaves of ideals such that `f^♯` sends `f^{-1}ℐ` into `ℐ'`. Three statements of the source are
about the interaction of `Rf_*` with derived completion along such ideals:

* [Stacks, Tag 099K]: `Rf_*` sends `D_comp(𝒪', ℐ')` into `D_comp(𝒪, ℐ)`, and the resulting
  functor `D_comp(𝒪', ℐ') ⥤ D_comp(𝒪, ℐ)` has a left adjoint `Lf^*_comp`, namely `Lf^*`
  followed by derived completion.
* [Stacks, Tag 0A0G] and the equation it justifies, [Stacks, Tag 0A0I]: `Rf_*` commutes with
  derived completion, `Rf_*(K^∧) = (Rf_*K)^∧`.
* [Stacks, Tag 099N], which is the list of both of these together with two `R lim` formulas, in
  the special case of constant Noetherian coefficients. Parts (1), (2) and (3) of that tag are
  registered in this file, part (3) only at a derived-complete object; its two `R lim` formulas,
  parts (4) and (5), are `PushforwardAdicLimit.lean` of this directory.

This file builds the three clauses of Tag 099K for a morphism of ringed *sites*, each for every
`ℐ'` whose derived-complete objects are reflective in `D(𝒪')`, and, of Tag 0A0G, the canonical
comparison map together with a criterion for it to be invertible. The `@[stacks 099K]`
registrations are on the statements for a morphism of ringed *topoi*, in
`PushforwardCompletionTopos.lean`:
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.isDerivedComplete_derivedPushforward` for the first
statement and, for an `ℐ'` of finite type,
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposHom.derivedCompletePullbackPushforwardAdjunction` for the second.
What is not in *this* file is the source's local computation showing Tag 0A0G's comparison map is
always invertible. That computation is carried out elsewhere in the directory, and Tag 0A0G is
proved at the source's own data — a sheaf of ideals `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪` of **finite type** and
`ℐ' = f^{-1}ℐ · 𝒪_X`, for an **arbitrary** object of `D(𝒪')` — by
`RingedSite.isIso_derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison_inverseImageIdealSheaf_of_isFiniteType`
of `PushforwardCommutesCompletionLocalToGlobal.lean`, which localizes the globally generated case
of `PushforwardCommutesCompletionCanonical.lean` along a covering family on whose members `ℐ` is
generated by finitely many sections. `PushforwardCommutesCompletionDisplay.lean` then reads that
invertibility as the commutation of functors Tag 0A0G is phrased as and as the isomorphism
`(Rf_*K)^∧ ≅ Rf_*(K^∧)` of Equation 52.7.0.1. So the criterion below is a stepping stone, not the
library's last word on the tag: its hypothesis is discharged in general there.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCompletePushforward`: `Rf_*` as a functor
  `D_comp(𝒪', ℐ') ⥤ D_comp(𝒪, ℐ)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCompletePullback`: `Lf^*_comp`, that is `Lf^*` followed by
  derived completion, as a functor `D_comp(𝒪, ℐ) ⥤ D_comp(𝒪', ℐ')`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.completedPushforwardOfDerivedCompletion`: `K ↦ Rf_*(K^∧)`, read
  as a functor into the derived-complete objects of `D(𝒪)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.pushforwardDerivedCompletionUnit`: the natural map
  `Rf_*K ⟶ Rf_*(K^∧)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison`: the canonical natural
  map `(Rf_*K)^∧ ⟶ Rf_*(K^∧)`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCompletePullbackPushforwardAdjunction`: the adjunction of
  **Tag 099K**, `Lf^*_comp ⊣ Rf_*` on the derived-complete objects, for a reflective
  `D_comp(𝒪', ℐ')`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedComplete_derivedPushforward_derivedCompletion`:
  `Rf_*(K^∧)` is derived complete.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCompletionUnit_comp_derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison`:
  the comparison map is the one the universal property of derived completion produces, i.e. it
  is compatible with the two units.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison_of_isIso_map_unit`:
  the comparison map `(Rf_*K)^∧ ⟶ Rf_*(K^∧)` is invertible as soon as `Rf_*(K ⟶ K^∧)` is.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isIso_derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison_of_isDerivedComplete`:
  in particular it is invertible at a derived-complete `K`, where
  `Rf_*(K^∧) = Rf_*K = (Rf_*K)^∧`.

## Implementation notes

*The reflector of Tag 099F.* The source's Tag 099K reads "`ℐ'` of finite type", and uses that
hypothesis only through [Stacks, Tag 099F], to know that `D_comp(𝒪', ℐ') ⥤ D(𝒪')` has a left
adjoint. The statements here ask for exactly that conclusion,
`(ObjectProperty.ι (AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.IsDerivedComplete X I')).IsRightAdjoint`, and
so apply at every `ℐ'` for which it is known, rather than at the finite-type `ℐ'` from which the
source derives it. Three declarations of this library establish it:
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_idealOfGlobalSections` of
`CompletionIdempotent.lean`, for an ideal sheaf generated by finitely many global sections, with
the Čech complex of those sections as the adjoint;
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_of_eq_idealOfGlobalSections` of
`FiniteTypeGlobalSections.lean`, for any ideal sheaf equal to such a one; and
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete_zeroSubmodule` of
`Reflection.lean`, for the zero sheaf of ideals.

Most generally, for an `ℐ'` of finite type, it is the instance
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isRightAdjoint_ι_isDerivedComplete` of `FiniteTypeReflector.lean`,
[Stacks, Tag 099F] at the source's generality, so the statements here then apply with no
further argument.

*The adjunction.* Three inputs: `Lf^* ⊣ Rf_*` of [Stacks, Tag 07A6], here the declaration
`derivedPullbackPushforwardAdjunctionOfFlatPullback` of the namespace
`Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedPullbackPushforwardAdjunction`, fed with [Stacks, Tag 05VD] in the
shape `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedToposSiteHom.pullbackPreservesIsFlatUniv`;
the reflector `(-)^∧ ⊣ ι` of `ReflectorCompletion.lean`; and
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedPushforward_isDerivedComplete`, which is
[Stacks, Tag 099J] and is what makes `Rf_*` restrict at all. The composite of the first two
adjunctions is an adjunction between `D(𝒪)` and `D_comp(𝒪')`, and
`CategoryTheory.Adjunction.restrictReflective` cuts it down to `D_comp(𝒪)` on the left using
the full faithfulness of the inclusion. This is exactly the source's chain
`Hom(K, Rf_*M) = Hom(Lf^*K, M) = Hom(Lf^*_comp K, M)`.

*The comparison map.* Rather than an object-wise adjunct, the comparison is built as a mate, so
that naturality is free: the natural map `β : Rf_* ⟶ (-)^∧ ⋙ Rf_*` is `Rf_*` whiskered onto the
unit `K ⟶ K^∧` of the source, its target factors through the derived-complete objects of `D(𝒪)`
by Tag 099J, and the comparison is `β` whiskered with the reflector and then composed with the
counit of the reflector adjunction. The resulting natural transformation
`Rf_* ⋙ (-)^∧ ⟶ (-)^∧ ⋙ Rf_*` has components `(Rf_*K)^∧ ⟶ Rf_*(K^∧)`, and the identity
`derivedCompletionUnit_comp_derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison` says it is the unique such
map compatible with the units — which is how the source introduces it.

### Where Tag 0A0G's invertibility is proved

The source proves the comparison map invertible by reducing to `ℐ` generated by global sections
`f_1, …, f_r` (via [Stacks, Tag 0A0F], localization and derived completion), rewriting both
sides with the Koszul formula `K^∧ = R lim (K ⊗^L K_n)` of [Stacks, Tag 0A0E], exchanging `Rf_*`
with `R lim`, and finishing with the projection formula [Stacks, Tag 0944] and
`Lf^*K(𝒪, f_1^n, …, f_r^n) = K(𝒪', g_1^n, …, g_r^n)`. Of these four inputs, the first three are
now available and the last two steps are not:

* Tag 0A0F, the reduction step, is `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.derivedCompletion_restrict` of
  `LocalizationCompletionFiniteType.lean`, for `ℐ` of finite type.
* Tag 0A0E is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedLimit_tensorDerivedDualSystem_koszulPowerSystem_canonical`
  of `KoszulCechHomotopyColimit.lean`: the completion of an ideal sheaf generated by finitely
  many global sections *is* a derived limit of the Koszul tower. (`R lim` is the predicate
  `CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.IsDerivedLimit` of [Stacks, Tag 08TC] rather than a functor,
  which is all the argument uses.)
* Tag 0A07, that `Rf_*` commutes with `R lim`, is
  `Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedPushforwardOnRingedTopoi.isDerivedLimit_map_derivedPushforward` of
  `StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/Sites/Cohomology/DerivedPushforward/DerivedLimits.lean`.
* **Tag 0944 is the obstruction, and inside it the base case is.** The map is
  `Stacks.Cohomology.ProjectionFormulaOnRingedTopoi.projectionFormulaMap` of
  [Stacks, Tag 0B56]; the dévissage in the complex on the base is carried out on a ringed topos
  in `StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/Sites/Cohomology/DerivedTensor/ProjectionFormulaPerfect.lean`, by
  `isIso_projectionFormulaMap_of_isStrictlyPerfect` of the namespace
  `Stacks.Cohomology.ProjectionFormulaPerfectDevissage`, and the Koszul complex is strictly perfect
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isStrictlyPerfect_koszulPowerComplex`), so the dévissage is
  enough — but it takes the base case as the hypothesis
  `hunit : ∀ i n, IsIso (projectionFormulaMap … ((singleUnit Y.O i)⟦n⟧))`, and nothing
  discharges it. The base case is
  `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectionFormula.isIso_adjunctionTensorMap_unitObj`, and the
  inventory of its four inputs in `StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/Sites/Cohomology/DerivedTensor/ProjectionFormulaPerfect.lean` now stands as
  follows.

  Three are available: the right unitors of the two derived tensor products
  (`Stacks.DerivedTensor.RingedSite.DerivedTensorProduct.rightUnitIso`, [Stacks, Tag 0FPT]) and
  the naturality of the one on the target of `Lf^*`; and the unit comparison
  `ν : Lf^*(𝒪[0]) ≅ 𝒪'[0]`, which
  `Stacks.Sheaves.DerivedPullback.isIso_derivedPullbackUnitMap_unconditional`
  reduces to the invertibility of the *ordinary* comparison
  `SheafOfModules.pullbackObjUnitToUnit f.fSharpRing`. That invertibility is *unconditional* for
  a morphism of ringed topoi presented by a morphism of sites, by cancellation in
  `Stacks.Sheaves.DerivedPullback.pullbackModulesSiteIso_hom_app_unit_comp_pullbackObjUnitToUnit`
  of `StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/Sites/Cohomology/DerivedPullback/PullbackToposUnitComparison.lean`, which identifies it with the inverse of
  the corepresentability isomorphism
  `Stacks.Sheaves.RingedToposModules.pullbackModulesObjUnitIso` of [Stacks, Tag 03LU]: it is an
  isomorphism composed with it, so it is one. Mathlib proves it only for a `Final` presenting
  functor (`SheafOfModules.pullbackObjUnitToUnit`), and no declaration of this library records
  the unconditional form, so the inventory still lists it as a hypothesis beyond the source's;
  it is not one.

  The fourth is missing, and is the whole of what blocks the base case: the right-unitor
  coherence of [Stacks, Tag 07A4] **in the derived category**. Its module-level form is proved,
  unconditionally in the morphism of sites, by
  `Stacks.Sheaves.DerivedPullback.pullbackToposRightUnitorCoherence` of
  `StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/Sites/Cohomology/DerivedPullback/PullbackToposRightUnitorCoherence.lean`, which inhabits the proposition
  `Stacks.Sheaves.DerivedPullback.PullbackToposRightUnitorCoherence` that
  `StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/Sites/Cohomology/DerivedPullback/PullbackToposUnitorCoherence.lean` states. What is owed is the passage from it
  to the derived statement: `𝒪[0]` is K-flat with flat terms, so the comparison of
  [Stacks, Tag 07A4] at it is computed degreewise by
  `Stacks.Sheaves.DerivedPullback.pullbackToposTensorTotalIso`, and the derived right unitor is
  computed by `rightUnitIso_hom_eq`; assembling those into the derived coherence is the one
  remaining step, and no declaration does it. (The discharged base case
  `Stacks.Cohomology.DerivedProjectionFormula.isIso_projectionFormulaMap_unitObject`,
  [Stacks, Tag 08EU], is for ringed *spaces*.)
* The identification `Lf^*K(𝒪, f_1^n, …, f_r^n) = K(𝒪', g_1^n, …, g_r^n)` is also absent: no
  statement of this library computes the derived pullback of
  `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.koszulPowerComplex`, and there is no construction carrying a
  family of global sections of `𝒪` to the family `g_i = f^♯(f_i)` on the source at the level of
  Koszul complexes. Nothing deeper than the previous item stands in its way: the Koszul complex
  is a bounded complex whose terms are finite products of `𝒪` — finite direct sums, the index
  sets being the subsets of `{1, …, r}` of a given cardinality — and whose differentials are
  matrices of multiplications by monomials in the `f_i`, and it is K-flat with flat terms
  (`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isStrictlyPerfect_koszulPowerComplex`), so `Lf^*` at it is the
  degreewise `f^*`, which is `f^*𝒪 ≅ 𝒪'` in each summand — the unconditional comparison recorded
  in the previous item — and the differentials match because `f^♯` is a map of sheaves of rings.
  It is an unperformed construction rather than a missing input.

So the obstruction is a single one: the right-unitor coherence of [Stacks, Tag 07A4] in the
derived category, which is what the base case of [Stacks, Tag 0944] waits on and therefore what
the general case of Tag 0A0G — and so part (3) of [Stacks, Tag 099N] — waits on. Everything
else in the source's proof is available or is an unperformed construction over available inputs,
including the locality of invertibility in `D(𝒪)` that the reduction to global generators needs
(`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isIso_of_coversTop_mapDerivedCategory`, [Stacks, Tag 08JJ]). The
criterion proved here, `isIso_derivedCompletionPushforwardComparison_of_isIso_map_unit`, is what
that computation would be fed into.

